A||N||1||KissMySSFiero||suspension bushing sleaves?  anyone ever damaged them? ||||1||
Z||000000||KissMySSFiero||08-13-2001||09:35 AM||||i havent damage any yet.  for the upper conrol arm(88)  i have to replace the UCA shaft.  to get the old one out i can cut it or i can take the sleave out to remove it.  im afraid ill damage the old sleave and the poly bushings dont come with new sleaves.  is there a replacement for these sleaves?  if so where is it?  thanks for the help.<BR><P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leadfoot||08-13-2001||10:08 AM||||There are two ways you can take out the old rubber bushings without damaging the sleeves.  One is to torch the bushing material until it burns away (too long and smelly).  The other way is to use a set of sockets and a table vise.  The trick is to try and press the inner bolt sleeve out.  This will make removing the rubber from the sleeve a piece of cake.  All you need is to place one socket that is a little smaller than the sleeve i.d. on one side, and place another socket a little smaller than the bolt sleeve o.d. on the other side and squeeze them in your vise.  I hope this is clear enough.<P>||||reg||1
